.TH RPOEM 6.SH NAMErpoem \- write verses at random.SH SYNOPSIS\fBrpoem\fR[count].SH DESCRIPTION\fBrpoem\fRwrites\fIcount\fRnumbered verses of four lines, thirty if no count is given, each builtat random from a grammar and a word list:.nf    A frail lark must gurgle under the motion of a wagon wheel    And worship a pensive petal.    But a pensive dove pursues power of time    While the motion of a wagon wheel reveres the frail lark..fi.SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/SNOBOL/RPOEM.SYN\fRthe grammar and vocabulary..TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/SNOBOL/PHRASE.SYN\fRphrases shared with the other programs of the set..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fROne of Robert Heller's programs translated from SNOBOL4 into C, fromJames F. Gimpel's\fIAlgorithms in SNOBOL4\fR;\fR\fBDOC/snobol\fRdescribes the set and\fBSRC/effo_snobol\fRholds the source..SH SEE ALSOrstory, spew